                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "As much as I would love to recommend this game, I cannot.  While I enjoyed the character interactions over all, the way some scenes ended abruptly, and the way the story itself 'ended' without resolution, are just too much of a negative.\n\nI would like to assume that the creator is planning to add more to the game story-wise because - \"The Stargazers is a self contained story, and while we’re open to the idea of making more stories in the future, we’re designing Stargazers around self-contained adventures for the Stargazers Squadron in the style of pulp fiction.\"  According to the description, but there is no ending, the story stops dead without any resolution or answers, it's a cliffhanger in the worst way.  If this is all that they are planning to have for this game, I cannot recommend purchasing this game at all, it is unfinished and very short, the 4.6 hours of playtime I have listed on this don't even include continuous play, a portion of it is simply idle time that I had left the game running for.\n\nTLDR: The game is short, unfinished and not worth purchasing in it's current state.   I sadly cannot recommend this game.",
